possible solutions to the gap equation, i.e., three different Gribov parameters, two of which can be eliminated by the regime of the theory. In addition, our conclusion about the regime of the theory is different from the literature. We also show that, in our case, there is no weak-coupling regime.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"APS"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"In this paper, we solve the gap equation of the Yang-Mills-Gribov-Zwanziger-Chern-Simon theory by considering the first order in the Chern-Simon topological mass term, $M$. As a result, we find three possible solutions to the gap equation, i.e. three different Gribov parameters. In addition, we analyze the regime of the theory for each of these Gribov parameters and we obtain a different result from the literature.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"control_number":1864188,"dois":[{"material":"publication","source":"APS","value":"10.1103/PhysRevD.105.094016"},{"material":"publication","source":"arXiv","value":"10.1103/PhysRevD.105.094016"}],"preprint_date":"2021-05-19","arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["hep-th"],"value":"2105.09133"}],"titles":[{"source":"APS","title":"Implications of the topological Chern-Simons mass in the gap equation"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"Implications of the Topological Chern-Simons mass in the Gap Equation"}],"document_type":["article"]},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1864188?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1864188?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1864188?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1864188?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1864188?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1864188?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1864188"},"updated":"2023-11-23T12:29:12.186634+00:00","created":"2021-05-20T00:00:00+00:00"}],"total":1},"links":{"sel